Research: .collab/research/2026-10-16-t3-code-c2c-support.md and live receipt JSON. Quality: preserve existing codebase architecture; small typed interfaces; meaningful regression and failure tests; no mock-only delivery claims; no whole-tree refactor; independent review/fix loop before merge. Decisions and evidence must be appended through bl. In upstream T3 source add an opt-in per-thread mailbox with persistent identity binding, accept-before-ack ingestion, idempotency, bounded retry and ambiguous-delivery holding, event-driven broker arrival plus startup reconciliation. Isolate c2c process calls; no shell interpolation or provider/session tokens in durable binding. Do not use ordinary thread_send for DATA.

Lane: T3 new c2c domain services and migration 63 only. Parent owns lifecycle/config/MCP; provider lane owns peerData types. Reuse ProcessRunner, SqlClient and scoped watchers. No duplicated process/queue machinery.